Notable toolchain issue found and worked around:
  dxc v1.10.2605.37 ships a native `frexp` intrinsic whose SPIR-V lowering is broken
  (OpConvertSToF on a non-int input -> "generated SPIR-V is invalid").  The game predates that
  intrinsic and defines a custom frexp in curve.hlsl.  curve.hlsl therefore defines the function
  as `incb_frexp` and adds `#define frexp incb_frexp` so consumer source-level `frexp(x, out e)`
  calls still resolve to the custom implementation.  (See curve.hlsl header note.)
